SOAPBOX: I am in the process of selling the house located on a mountaintop in WV where my K3ZJ station has been located for the past 38 years. All antennas already are dismantled. I decided to make "a few last QSOs for fun" after a last-minute trip to show the property to a potential buyer. I still had stored at the house my "travel" station: an EFHW for 10-80 meters, FTdx10, and SPE Expert 1.5K-FA. So I hung the EFHW with the feed point at 32-feet high and the other end at about 10-feet high tied to a tree branch. This worked so much better than I expected that I operated much more than ever intended -- 36 hours total. And I am claiming the record using a single MyAntennas 8010-2K EFHW antenna -- 1.34 million points raw score. It's the other stations with good antennas like I used to enjoy that did the heavy lifting on this one, thanks for the QSOs!
CREATED-BY: N1MM Logger+ 1.0.11469.0
